Troubleshooting
Issue: Indexes Not Being Used
Solution:

-- Update table statistics
ANALYZE users;
ANALYZE orders;

-- Rebuild indexes if needed
REINDEX TABLE orders;
Issue: Configuration Changes Not Applied
Solution:

# Check PostgreSQL status
sudo systemctl status postgresql

# View error logs
sudo tail -f /var/log/postgresql/postgresql-*-main.log

# Verify config file syntax
sudo -u postgres postgres -C shared_buffers
Issue: Out of Memory Errors
Solution:

-- Reduce work_mem temporarily
SET work_mem = '16MB';

-- Or modify for session
ALTER DATABASE perflab SET work_mem = '16MB';
Issue: Slow Query Despite Indexes
Checklist:

Verify index exists: \d table_name
Check if statistics are updated: ANALYZE table_name;
Ensure query uses indexed columns in WHERE clause
Avoid functions on indexed columns: WHERE LOWER(email) prevents index use
